Z||000000||chris6878||06-14-2000||04:48 PM||||I was looking in the engine bay of my fiero last nite. I noticed my manifolds where glowing just a little. Enough to where you could tell they where redish. I havent noticed this before, maybe i just wasnt looking. I dont have a cat converter on the car, just straight exhaust with muffler. It does burn gas rich if that would have anything to do with it.<P>TIA,<BR>chris||||reg||5
Z||000001||ThatRickGuy||06-14-2000||05:52 PM||||couple things to check (this is so much easier on old cars... ugg, computers...)<BR>first place to look, coolant, is there any? follow that long drawn out procedure to refill it (ya know, with lifting up the back of the car and what not to get the air out).<BR>The fuel/air mixture could also be the problem, back in the day it was a matter of messing with a carb, I have no idea on the EFI tho. and last but not least...Timing, with the spark hitting at the wrong time you can get some really strange things going on, one of which is glowing manifolds.<P>hope it works out for ya.||||reg||1
